+/* Six candidate ways to hand a command to the drive.
+ *
+ * Every disc so far tested one guess of mine, and every one of them was
+ * wrong, which is a poor use of somebody else's CD-Rs. So the guessing
+ * moves into the firmware: it tries each of these in turn and keeps
+ * whichever one the drive demonstrably answers. Six wrong guesses then
+ * cost one disc instead of six -- and six failures would be worth as
+ * much as any success, because that eliminates the whole idea that the
+ * trigger is a write being done in the wrong order or the wrong width.
+ *
+ * They differ in two things: whether the ten nibbles go down as five
+ * words or ten bytes, and what is done to HOCK afterwards. HOCK is
+ * documented as "starts communication with the CDD", which reads as a
+ * strobe -- and a strobe needs an edge, which writing an already-set
+ * bit does not produce. Taking it low also writes 0 to DTS and DRS,
+ * documented as aborting a transfer, so it only happens when the
+ * caller has just checked that neither is running. */
